From 40e9f940d53cd5d1fbd199150732261a9e3d902c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:32:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 70/76] v2-rc5: defer ring-block free under overlapping steps;
 count skipped ring commits (T.1c)

rc5 = rc4 (b75d0fe00e) + the two pre-fix commits of the v2.1 ring-row work
(T.1c), pulled into v2 by the operator on 2026-09-16.

1. Scheduler: enable defer_block_free whenever max_concurrent_batches > 1
   and any KV group carries a CircularBufferSpec layer (the QSA raw-key
   ring, one block per request, rewritten every step). Before, deferral
   needed a KV-consumer connector, so under TP2xPP2 a preempted/finished
   request's ring block could be handed to a new request while an in-flight
   step was still committing the old request's suffix rows (T.1a candidate
   C2). Same fence and drain as the connector gate.

   Review finding (Luna, P1): with deferral, a preempted victim returns no
   blocks until its step is processed, so the running-queue allocate loop
   retried, preempted the next victim, and with every running request in
   flight emptied the whole batch, requester included. The loop now stops
   after one deferred victim; the requester stays running, unscheduled,
   and retries after the drain. test_deferred_victim_stops_the_preemption_
   cascade fails on the previous loop ("the cascade reached the requester")
   and passes here.

2. Pre-indexer telemetry: a live token whose state slot is < 0 or beyond the
   ring capacity had its suffix commit silently masked away (T.1a candidate
   C1). The writer loop now counts those tokens into the new guard-telemetry
   site SITE_QSA_RING_SKIP (10; NUM_SITES 11; warn only, not fatal; slot 1 =
   max token index, slot 2 = max offending slot value). The skip itself is
   unchanged - the reconciliation is v2.1 T.1b.

Tests: tests/v1/core/test_deferred_block_free.py +5 (ring gate on/off,
dense-without-connector off, ring preempt withholds the block until the
fence, the cascade); tests/v1/worker/gpu/test_qsa_ring_skip_telemetry.py
(site declared/named/not fatal, launcher wiring, GPU negative control, three
positive controls at slot -1 / capacity / past capacity checking the whole
row, two-token accumulation). Box CPU run: 21 passed, 12 GPU tests deferred
to the rc5 re-qualification; test_scheduler.py + test_async_scheduler.py
failure set identical before/after (pre-existing venv config issue).
